	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105038705314?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {This study aims to explore the impact of personalized news recommendation systems based on big data and artificial intelligence algorithms on audience cognition and behavior. With the rapid development of information technology, news recommendation systems have been widely used in the media industry, but their impact on audiences has not been fully studied. This paper adopts a mixed research method, combining questionnaire surveys, in-depth interviews and experimental research, and conducts a three-month follow-up survey on 500 news app users. The results show that the personalized recommendation system significantly increases users' news reading volume and retention time, but also leads to the intensification of information cocoon effect and cognitive bias. In addition, the study finds that the transparency of the recommendation algorithm, the user's media literacy level and the diversity of news sources are key factors affecting audience cognition and behavior. Based on the research findings, this paper proposes suggestions for optimizing the news recommendation system, improving users' media literacy and promoting information diversification, in order to minimize the negative impact of personalized recommendations while improving user experience. This study has important theoretical and practical significance for understanding the characteristics of audience behavior in the intelligent media environment, improving the design of news recommendation systems and formulating relevant policies. © The Authors. Published under.},
